cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "legal-ml-core"
abstract: >-
  legal-ml-core is the backend of the Legal Blocks / BAIGLE no-code machine
  learning workbench for legal text, packaged as an installable Flask
  extension. It provides dataset upload, validation and exploratory data
  analysis; model configuration, training, prediction and LIME/SHAP
  explanation for classical scikit-learn and transformer (LegalBERT, RoBERTa)
  models; visualization; annotation task queues; and experiment monitoring.
  The same SQLAlchemy models and compute engine are shared by the HTTP API
  process and a separate Redis-driven training worker. It is designed for
  teaching legal professionals and students machine learning without
  writing code.
